      "title": "Reject contradictory A3 evidence before committing a new unsupported terminal state",
      "evidence": "A3 normal local case is coherent: live dispatch moves an undispatched create to denied, request pending, no execution or runtime command, hence no claim/home/reservation. But line540 expressly says if any proof condition fails, steps1-3 stand: create denied, request failed/not_dispatched, and retire written, then delivered and acknowledged in full. The new test576 explicitly seeds a runtime command and requires that fallback. This new failed transition is caused by dispatch; it is neither a runtime receipt, capture, hello lease-loss transition nor A1 cancellation. B6 and unchanged frozen Q7r8:869 require a real causal terminalWriter of precisely those forms. A3:546 supplies its own rows only for the local no-runtime exemption, not for a delivered retirement. Q7r8:795-805/836/844 requires the barrier even for a proven-absent home. A later create receipt records an answer but cannot be called the record that already made this request failed; Q7r8:713,725-726 preserves an already-terminal request and provides no new writer. Thus the required seeded fallback has no supported terminalWriter and cannot truthfully finish its full barrier. A bare execution row without a runtime command additionally lacks the authenticated create scope at proposal282. This is an explicit proposal/test inconsistency on contradictory evidence, not proof that ordinary atomic dispatch reaches it.",
      "smallestCorrection": "Check every A3 proof condition under the existing project/outbox/request/binding locks before committing any A3 denial/failed/retire writes. If the proof is contradictory (an execution/runtime command already exists, or the expected create transition cannot happen), refuse the whole A3 transaction with a fixed CON-only diagnostic and no mutation; do not leave steps1-3 standing or promise full acknowledgement. Let existing delivered-create receipt/capture/hello/cancellation paths supply their real terminal writer and full retirement. Preserve the ordinary proved-never-dispatched A3 local case, its no-counter/no-call/no-fabricated-receipt rule, A1/A2 and the complete full barrier. A deliberate new dispatch-terminalWriter form would instead be a separately enumerated material addendum requiring its actual owners; it is not supplied by this review.",
      "futureQualification": "Keep grant-expired/asker-no-longer-writes/source-ineligible positive A3 cases with all four atomic writes, no runtime/create-answer/claim/reservation/cancellation/job/event, exact one retire and replay +0. Replace seeded-runtime fallback expectation with fixed refusal and transaction rollback: request/create command/outbox/attempt/binding/retire and any existing accounting unchanged. Add an execution-only contradictory seed and a failed expected-state transition; neither may retire locally, invent scope/writer, settle/release/reset an ordinal or create a call. Separately retain the genuine delivered-create-before-claim full-retirement case and verify its actual receipt/hello writer, real create answer, scrubbed payload, all eight predicates and process/relay proof. Under reachable pending, S2:311 forbids reserve before go; no unsafe-spend case is asserted. No test executed or new run authorized."
    }
  ],
